WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.735
-[ Whispering ] Alright,
be really -- Alright.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.137
Do you want to go get mommy now?
-I want to.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.271
-Tell her we're shooting
the show.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.439
Say, "We're shooting
the show, Mom."

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.641
-Mama?
-Yeah?

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:12.645
-We're taping the show.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.814
-Winnie, are you gonna sing?
-Yeah.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.316
Alright, is Franny
gonna hold the cake?

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.318
-Mm-hmm.
-Alright.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:23.856
-♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.458
-Alright, grab the cake.
Get the cake.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.260
Okay, perfect. Get the cake.
-Give it to me.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:33.232
-There you go. Go.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:34.433
-♪ Happy...♪

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:38.838
-You guys!

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.240
What?!
-Be careful, be careful.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:46.179
-♪ Happy birthday to you ♪
-What?!

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.381
In trouble.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:55.321
I love this!

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.090
-Finish. Sing it. Finish.
No, don't --

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.259
-Oh, wait.
We have to do some wishes.

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:03.830
Okay. Okay. Going in.
-Happy birthday!

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.801
We love you so much!
-Yay! I love you guys.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:10.737
-We love you so much.
-Thank you. Mwah!

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.938
-Happy, happy, happy --
-Thank you.

00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:15.708
I love you so much.
-And I love you, little ones.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:19.112
♪♪
-♪ We in the house ♪

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.479
-Come on!

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:23.416
-Tonight, join Jimmy
and his guests...

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.618
Arnold Schwarzenegger...

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.986
Cole Sprouse...

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:29.255
musical guest Billy Corgan...

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.691
and the legendary Roots crew.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.693
It's "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.595
-♪ We in the house, y'all ♪

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.497
-And now, here's Jimmy.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.698
-Hey, everybody.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.333
Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:46.405
It's special day here, because
it is my wife's birthday!

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:53.512
The producer, camera operator,
location scouter, editor.

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:54.981
Yeah, we love you, honey.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:58.784
And I know you don't like
surprises.

00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:00.219
Oh, yeah. Don't worry about it.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.254
You'll get
another cake later on, too.

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:04.357
But I won't tape that one.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:08.327
I will say, I did --
My dad got you a gift.

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:09.762
-Stop it.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:13.299
-[ Gasps ] No!

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.569
The best gift. No. Stop it.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:22.008
Oh, my God! Graber Olives.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.110
-My wife loves these olives.
-Best tradition in the world.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.578
-Yeah. Right?

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.812
I guess my mom
started doing it, too.

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.881
-Yep, she did.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:33.485
-Graber Olives is your favorite.
Why do you even -- They're good.

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:38.191
-Oh, don't! Don't speak.
-[ Laughing ] Don't speak.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:41.093
-Unless you love them,
no right to opinion.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.196
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.230
-I do love them.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.664
But, anyways,
that's from my dad.

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:47.433
Happy birthday.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.203
And, you know, I have gifts.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.470
I have things for you
and all that stuff.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.106
But I think you got
the best gift.

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:55.541
-I think I did.

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:58.344
-From --
-You can't even talk about it.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.345
-I can't
even talk about it.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.916
I'm so angry. Yeah.
Liza is awesome.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.784
Yeah, but she knows --
She's a producer.

00:03:05.784 --> 00:03:07.987
-She makes this show
that we love.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:10.055
-Yes, called "The Challenge."

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:11.491
We love MTV's "The Challenge."
We are the biggest.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.825
-Yeah.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:16.129
-And is our favorite --
It has to be Bananas, right?

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.330
-Yeah.
-Without a doubt.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.898
-I mean, not even --
-Yeah.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.833
-We have others we love.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.301
And there's others
we do not like.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.904
-Yes, there are others we
dislike as much as we love --

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.907
-Some human that we look forward
to seeing every single time

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.442
is Johnny Bananas.

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:32.979
I think he is funny. I love him.
I've always liked him.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:36.148
And, so, it's something --
But, anyways, you go,

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:37.650
"Dude, wait till you see this!

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.752
This is the best gift."
-I could not even teach today.

00:03:40.752 --> 00:03:42.688
-For homeschooling? No.
-Yeah.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:45.558
-Yeah, you were so geeked out.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.260
Our friend got Johnny Bananas to
do a personal message

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:52.765
for Nancy, for her birthday,
which is just untoppable.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.967
Anyways, here it is.

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.570
-Alright, this is a very special
happy-birthday

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.539
shout-out going
to my girl, Nancy,

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.640
coming to you from
your boy, Bananas.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.544
Nancy, may you live,
may you love,

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.478
and may your birthday
in quarantine

00:04:06.478 --> 00:04:09.882
be absolutely bananas.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.817
-Thank you, Johnny Bananas!
-Whoo-hoo!

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:14.353
-Come on! This is a lucky year.

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:15.722
-It is bananas.
-It's going to be a great year.

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.423
It's going to be a bananas year.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.459
Thank you, Johnny Bananas. Gosh.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:21.761
-And happy,
happy birthday, honey.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.363
I love you so much.
-I love you.

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:28.000
-I couldn't see you
from behind the camera, so...

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.570
Anyway, everybody, here we are.
This is Monday.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.073
And I want to thank everybody
for staying at home

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.707
and for washing your hands
and wearing a mask

00:04:35.707 --> 00:04:37.176
and doing all the right things.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:41.747
I know some states have been
slowly opening, which is great.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:43.883
And I want to say those states,
thank you

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.085
for not rubbing it in
to the states

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.686
that have to still stay home,

00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:49.589
because we want to do this
the right way.

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:52.024
And it's baby steps
and it's small steps,

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:55.394
and for those states
that have to stay in lockdown,

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:56.462
we're going the get there.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.998
And this is --
The hill is already over.

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.399
We're over the hill.
We're coming down.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:03.769
This is like --
This time is just

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:06.105
be safe and do it right,
get tested.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.506
There's lots of
testing out there.

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:10.743
If you can't get tested,
complain to someone.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.778
I'm sure there's someone
that can do something

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:15.381
and get you all tested
so we all can move forward.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.617
And I think I can see a light

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.685
at the end of
the tunnel here, guys.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:22.288
But thank you, everybody,
for doing what you're doing.

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:25.658
I know it feels like no one
is thanking you, probably.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:29.028
And it's probably 'cause
no one really is.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:33.632
But I am saying thank you
on behalf of my family --

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:35.134
my wife and my kids.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:42.508
Thank you so much for doing what
you can to -- I don't know.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:45.444
It's a tough thing.
This is rough.

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:48.714
But, you know, we're all doing
it together, right?

00:05:48.714 --> 00:05:49.982
In experiencing this stuff.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:53.318
So I like to support
whenever I can.

00:05:53.318 --> 00:05:55.588
Anyway, thank you
for doing that.

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:57.422
And thank you for supporting me
and watching the show.

00:05:57.422 --> 00:05:59.425
Thank you, NBC, for airing this.
YouTube. Who else?

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:01.260
-Thank you, thank you,
Johnny Bananas.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.195
-Johnny Bananas --
thank him again.

00:06:03.195 --> 00:06:04.963
Graber Olives, we want to thank.
-Yeah.

00:06:04.963 --> 00:06:07.733
-Fudgie the Whale
making a cameo.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.336
Fudgie the Whale making a cameo,
straight out of Carvel.

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:11.771
Alright, here we go.

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:14.172
Guys, here's some
potentially great news.

00:06:14.172 --> 00:06:16.542
Scientists working on
the coronavirus vaccine

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:19.111
announced positive results
in an early trial.

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:20.546
It's exciting.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:23.215
From here, the vaccine will go
through the blind auditions,

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:24.650
the battle rounds,
and then it does well there,

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:28.287
it's going to Hollywood!

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:30.723
During his briefing yesterday,
New York governor Andrew Cuomo

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.092
got a coronavirus test
live on TV

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.061
to show that it's no big deal.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.196
That's right --
they did the nasal swab,

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:38.964
and he said it was totally fine.

00:06:38.964 --> 00:06:40.433
Although, for the rest
of the briefing,

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:44.937
he did speak with a
British accent.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:47.339
[ British accent ]
New Yorkers are tough.

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:51.043
New Yorkers
have to stay together.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.444
[ Normal voice ]
Today, Governor Cuomo said

00:06:52.444 --> 00:06:56.082
New York sports teams should
plan to reopen without fans.

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:57.583
It will be so quiet,
the only sounds you'll hear

00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:00.353
are the crack of the bat,
the pop of the glove,

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:04.156
and the adjusting of
testicles rattling inside a cup.

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:07.760
Come on. Come on.

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:13.866
This weekend, during an
interview with Jeanine Pirro,

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:17.536
Eric trump accused Democrats of
milking coronavirus lockdowns

00:07:17.536 --> 00:07:19.905
to win the November election.

00:07:19.905 --> 00:07:22.341
Jeanine Pirro was like, "Yeah,
I totally agree with you.

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:24.309
It's definitely a hoax.

00:07:24.309 --> 00:07:25.745
Which is why we're doing
this interview

00:07:25.745 --> 00:07:27.980
from the basement of our homes."

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.252
Some TV news.

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:35.254
The last two episodes of
Michael Jordan's --

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:37.156
Oh, gosh.
This happens to me all the time.

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:40.059
The last two episodes
were last Sunday's.

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:41.694
I do this all the time.
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:41.694 --> 00:07:44.396
-Do you remember the biggest
game in the world? Game 5?

00:07:44.396 --> 00:07:45.565
It was, like, LeBron.

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:47.365
Everyone talked about
his best game ever?

00:07:47.365 --> 00:07:49.435
And I missed it because I
watched "Driving Miss Daisy"?

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:53.539
-Oh, yeah, that's right.

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:58.143
-No one e-mails me.
I don't have any sports friends.

00:07:58.143 --> 00:07:59.579
The world watched it.

00:07:59.579 --> 00:08:01.547
They said it's the best game
they ever seen in their life.

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:03.949
They could make an
ESPN docu-series of that.

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:06.151
I missed that because I go,
"You know what?"

00:08:06.151 --> 00:08:07.753
Oh, maybe you were here
or something.

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:11.290
You weren't at the apartment.
I go, "I got a night to myself.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.425
I've never seen
'Driving Miss Daisy.'

00:08:13.425 --> 00:08:16.095
I heard it's good."
It is great, by the way.

00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:17.363
Fantastic.
-It was a great movie.

00:08:17.363 --> 00:08:18.798
-Yeah.
-Mm-hmm.

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:22.168
-Was Patti LuPone in there?
Make a little cameo in there?

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:23.902
Maybe?

00:08:23.902 --> 00:08:25.805
It was a great movie, though.

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:29.174
Dan Aykroyd, props.
Anyways, loved the movie.

00:08:29.174 --> 00:08:33.846
Missed the best game in
the history of basketball.

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:35.347
Anyway, so, I missed
the Jordan thing last night.

00:08:35.347 --> 00:08:37.716
I watched Spade's movie.

00:08:37.716 --> 00:08:41.687
But, hey, I got time.
I have nothing but time, right?

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:43.656
-There's always tonight.

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:46.158
-Well, tonight,
it's birthday time.

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:48.493
Just tomorrow.
-So "Dateline" it is.

00:08:48.493 --> 00:08:52.230
-[ Laughs ] Oh, gosh.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.166
I can't watch "Dateline"
before I go to bed.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.801
Anyways, sorry. TV news.

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.603
Last two episodes of the
Michael Jordan docu-series

00:08:57.603 --> 00:08:59.438
"The Last Dance"
aired last night.

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:00.539
That's right.

00:09:00.539 --> 00:09:02.241
There was a lot of
unexpected moments,

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:04.644
especially at the end,
when Jordan was caught

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:10.082
on a live mic in the bathroom
confessing to three murders.

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:11.249
"I did it."

00:09:11.249 --> 00:09:13.252
That's a little
"Jinx" reference.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:17.356
Little "Jinx" reference.
Timely.

00:09:17.356 --> 00:09:20.326
Our monologue, you know,
sometimes is not necessarily

00:09:20.326 --> 00:09:21.427
the funniest thing
you've ever heard,

00:09:21.427 --> 00:09:24.163
but boy, oh, boy, is it topical.

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:26.265
You know?

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:28.333
A little "Jinx" reference.

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:30.202
In the documentary, Jordan
revealed that in his

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:32.805
legendary flu game,
he actually had food poisoning

00:09:32.805 --> 00:09:34.673
from eating an entire bad pizza.

00:09:34.673 --> 00:09:36.842
Yep, the food poisoning
was really rough on Jordan.

00:09:36.842 --> 00:09:39.744
Here he was before
the bad pizza.

00:09:39.744 --> 00:09:42.181
And here he is after.

00:09:42.181 --> 00:09:44.483
Come on. Papa John!

00:09:44.483 --> 00:09:45.684
Everyone is talking about this.

00:09:45.684 --> 00:09:47.786
Over the weekend,
Nelly and Ludacris tried to go

00:09:47.786 --> 00:09:49.721
head-to-head on Instagram Live,

00:09:49.721 --> 00:09:53.793
but Nelly's Wi-Fi was bad,
so he kept cutting out.

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:56.595
It was like listening to a
Lil Wayne song on Radio Disney.

00:09:56.595 --> 00:09:59.131
♪ I'm gonna...you up ♪

00:09:59.131 --> 00:10:02.167
♪ Then...your...face ♪

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:04.469
Wow. That's right --
the Wi-Fi issues

00:10:04.469 --> 00:10:05.904
were really frustrating
for fans.

00:10:05.904 --> 00:10:07.573
When Nelly got cut off,
they were like,

00:10:07.573 --> 00:10:11.910
"It's getting hot in where?

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:14.313
What? It's getting hot where?

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:17.883
It's getting hot in..."

00:10:17.883 --> 00:10:20.386
I saw that Graceland is
reopening this week.

00:10:20.386 --> 00:10:21.554
That's cool.

00:10:21.554 --> 00:10:22.822
When they heard that,
tourists were like,

00:10:22.822 --> 00:10:25.090
"After sitting on my couch
for two months,

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:29.595
I want to see where Elvis sat on
the couch for three years."

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:30.896
I read that some states,
like Hawaii,

00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:33.666
are asking tourists --
I love this.

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:35.367
Some states, like Hawaii,
are asking tourists

00:10:35.367 --> 00:10:37.236
to help them handle
the coronavirus outbreak

00:10:37.236 --> 00:10:40.039
by not visiting.

00:10:40.039 --> 00:10:42.108
That's right -- after years of
trying to attract visitors,

00:10:42.108 --> 00:10:44.075
now they're hoping
to keep them away.

00:10:44.075 --> 00:10:47.913
A few states even unveiled some
new tourism slogans.

00:10:47.913 --> 00:10:49.614
Check it out. First, Colorado.

00:10:49.614 --> 00:10:54.119
Their slogan is, "You can buy
weed everywhere else now, too."

00:10:54.119 --> 00:10:56.088
Next up, North Carolina.

00:10:56.088 --> 00:11:00.793
Their new slogan is, "Trust us,
South Carolina is way nicer."

00:11:00.793 --> 00:11:02.394
Then there's South Carolina.

00:11:02.394 --> 00:11:04.496
Their new slogan is,
"No, no, no.

00:11:04.496 --> 00:11:07.332
North Carolina is
by far the best."

00:11:07.332 --> 00:11:08.533
Then there's New Jersey.

00:11:08.533 --> 00:11:12.204
Their new slogan is,
"Get outta here!"

00:11:12.204 --> 00:11:13.539
Next is Minnesota.

00:11:13.539 --> 00:11:16.342
Their slogan is, "It takes
40 hours to drive here

00:11:16.342 --> 00:11:18.143
no matter where you leave from."

00:11:18.143 --> 00:11:20.679
That will deter tourists.

00:11:20.679 --> 00:11:23.315
And, finally, there's
Washington, who says,

00:11:23.315 --> 00:11:25.584
"We're basically
Canada's armpit."

00:11:25.584 --> 00:11:27.519
Well, that will keep
tourists away.

00:11:27.519 --> 00:11:28.587
Well, listen to this.

00:11:28.587 --> 00:11:31.456
A new study found that
Jonah Hill

00:11:31.456 --> 00:11:35.227
has cursed in movies
more than any other film actor.

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:39.732
Yeah, at 376 curses,
Jonah slightly edged out

00:11:39.732 --> 00:11:43.202
Samuel L. Jackson
and Dame Maggie Smith.

00:11:43.202 --> 00:11:45.671
Congratulations, Jonah.

00:11:45.671 --> 00:11:47.272
I read about a new line
of nail polish

00:11:47.272 --> 00:11:50.542
that smells like taco, pizza,
and cheese puffs.

00:11:50.542 --> 00:11:52.010
Meanwhile, Americans are like,

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:53.579
"We've been quarantined
for over two months.

00:11:53.579 --> 00:11:58.550
Our fingers already smell like
tacos, pizza, and cheese puffs."

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.452
And, finally, a man in
North Carolina just won

00:12:00.452 --> 00:12:02.755
$10 million on
a scratch-off ticket

00:12:02.755 --> 00:12:04.523
and said once
the pandemic is over,

00:12:04.523 --> 00:12:07.827
he's taking his family
on a cruise.

00:12:07.827 --> 00:12:09.361
When they heard,
his family grabbed his ticket

00:12:09.361 --> 00:12:10.830
and ripped it up.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.031
What's wrong with that man?

00:12:12.031 --> 00:12:13.131
That is our monologue,
everybody.

00:12:13.131 --> 00:12:14.233
Thank you very much.

